.TE
.sp
The following example reserves a new event ID for an origin defined in
\fBorigin.xml\fP\&. It is assumed that \fBscevent\fP is configured with
\fBrestAPI = 18182\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
curl \-v \-X POST http://localhost:18182/api/1/allocate \-H \(dqContent\-Type: text/xml\(dq \-d @origin.xml
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The reserved ID is cached (and, if \fI\%eventIDSync.db\fP is set, persisted) exactly
as in the \fBallocate\fP mode of \fI\%try\-to\-associate\fP, so a
repeated request for the same origin returns the same reserved ID rather than allocating
a second one.
