\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBeventIDSync.*\fP
\fIParameters controlling the synchronization of event IDs between several\fP
\fIdistributed :program:\(gascevent\(ga instances deployed for redundancy. One\fP
\fIinstance is designated the main instance and allocates event IDs on\fP
\fIbehalf of all the secondary instances; each secondary instance asks the\fP
\fImain instance via its REST API before creating a new event so that all\fP
\fIinstances converge on the same ID for the same earthquake.\fP
**
\fIWhen :confval:\(gaeventIDSync.main\(ga is empty this instance acts as a main\fP
\fIinstance (or as a standalone instance if no secondary instance ever\fP
\fIconnects). When set, it acts as a secondary instance. See\fP
\fI:ref:\(gascevent\-eventid\-sync\(ga in the documentation for the full mechanism,\fP
\fIincluding the /api/1/try\-to\-associate?allocate endpoint used internally\fP
\fIfor the handshake and the /api/1/allocate endpoint used for the\fP
\fIsplit\-origin and forced new\-event commands.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eventIDSync.main
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
URL of the main instance\(aqs REST API, for example
\(dq\fI\%http://event\-main.example.org:18182\fP\(dq. Leave empty to make this
instance a main instance (or a standalone instance). When set, this
instance acts as a secondary instance and asks the configured main
instance for an event ID before creating a new event. If the main
instance cannot be reached within \fI\%eventIDSync.mainTimeout\fP
seconds the secondary instance falls back to local event ID
allocation.
.sp
The URL may include an explicit path; if no path is given,
\(dq/api/1/try\-to\-associate\(dq is used. Both \(dqhttp\(dq and \(dqhttps\(dq schemes
are supported.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eventIDSync.mainTimeout
Default: \fB5\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
Maximum number of seconds a secondary instance waits for the main
instance\(aqs response before falling back to local event ID
allocation. Only effective when \fI\%eventIDSync.main\fP is set.
Must be greater than zero.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eventIDSync.cacheRetention
Default: \fB1800\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
Number of seconds a main instance keeps a reserved event ID in its
in\-memory cache, together with the foreign origin that triggered the
reservation. While the entry is cached, a local origin matching that
foreign origin is assigned the same event ID instead of allocating a
new one. After this time the entry is dropped from the cache and the
event ID may be reused by subsequent allocations. Must be greater
than zero.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eventIDSync.db
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Path to an SQLite database file used by a main instance to keep the
event IDs it reserves on behalf of secondary instances beyond the
lifetime of the in\-memory cache. When empty (the default) the
reservations live only in memory and are lost when scevent restarts.
When set, reservations survive restarts and may cover a much larger
origin/event\-ID set than the in\-memory cache: on a try\-to\-associate
request the main instance looks up the incoming origin both by its
public ID (fast path) and by a windowed epicenter/shared\-pick
comparison over all stored origins around the incoming origin time
(bounded by \fI\%eventAssociation.eventTimeBefore\fP and
\fI\%eventAssociation.eventTimeAfter\fP), mirroring the strategy
used against the SeisComP database. Only relevant in main mode
(\fI\%eventIDSync.main\fP empty).
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eventIDSync.databaseRetention
Default: \fB\-1\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
Number of seconds a reserved event ID is kept in the persistent
database given by \fI\%eventIDSync.db\fP, measured by origin
time. Should be at least as large as
\fI\%eventIDSync.cacheRetention\fP; a larger value lets the main
instance keep answering secondary\-instance requests for older
origins after a restart. Rows older than this are pruned at startup
and periodically at runtime. A negative value (the default)
disables pruning, keeping reservations indefinitely.
.UNINDENT
